<%# The one-time reveal (design spec §6.1, Task 9) -- rendered straight from
    `Admin::ApiTokensController#create`, served `no-store`; see that
    action's own comment for why nothing else ever holds the raw token.
    This is a whole document (the create form posts with
    `data-turbo="false"`, fix round 1), so its `<head>` can carry
    `turbo-cache-control: no-cache` from the very first byte: Turbo never
    snapshots this page, so leaving it (any link) and coming Back refetches
    the list instead of restoring the reveal. A frame-rendered reveal
    couldn't guarantee that -- Turbo's promoted frame visit caches snapshots
    (and fires `turbo:before-cache`) on its own schedule, which either kept
    the reveal in the cache or, with `data-turbo-temporary`, removed it from
    the live page right after it rendered.
    `admin--token-reveal` does the copying (Clipboard API, falling back to
    selecting the text) and blanks the token on `pagehide` for the
    browser's own back/forward cache. Round 3 draws it as the AI assistant
    page itself (the warn box in step 1, the token in step 2's configuration),
    listing the new token in the table beneath. %>
<% content_for :title, "AI assistant" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="turbo-cache-control" content="no-cache">
<% end %>
<%= render "admin/api_tokens/screen", raw_token: @raw_token %>
